  "title": "Sales Team Compensation",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "company": "Oracle",
  "premium": true,
  "question": "As the Sales Operations Analyst at Oracle, you must help the VP of Sales work out the final compensation earned by each salesperson for the year. The structure is a fixed base salary, a commission based on total deals, and possible accelerators for beating quota.\n\nEach salesperson earns a fixed base salary plus a percentage commission on their total deals. If they beat their quota, any sales after that receive an accelerator: a higher commission rate applied to the commissions after they hit the quota.\n\nWrite a query that calculates total compensation per salesperson. Output the employee ID and total compensation, sorted in descending order; in the case of ties, sort employee IDs ascending.",
  "notes": [],
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "employee_contract",
      "columns": [
